Fair. I didn''t mean he''s scamming anybody. It''s the "dead end" thing that gets me, because my weekend guy clearly isn''t one.';  -- T022/r3
update replies set body = 'Since the first thing everyone asks is what changed: the interview. I had real jobs to talk about the third time. Before that I had nothing. And yes, I retook the test each time. Idk if that''s required everywhere, ask the program directly.' where id = 'a97340b3-975f-5ffa-a6be-18a92eece5c6' and seed_batch_id = 'fm-2026-10' and body = 'The interview. I had real jobs to talk about the third time. Before that I had nothing.';  -- T029/r1
update replies set body = 'For anyone wondering whether to bring up a third try: they knew. I said it before they could. Then I said what I did differently each year.' where id = '63a042cc-4155-5c7d-98a8-6c89a4c7bc83' and seed_batch_id = 'fm-2026-10' and body = 'They knew. I said it before they could. Then I said what I did differently each year.';  -- T029/r14
update replies set body = 'Thanks everyone, didn''t expect this many replies.' where id = '9acc57e0-922b-5d67-b9af-054f1db5e4c3' and seed_batch_id = 'fm-2026-10' and body = 'Will do. Thanks everyone, didn''t expect this many questions tonight.';  -- T029/r18
update replies set body = 'For anyone wondering if they let you do anything on these: mostly watching. On the electrical one he had me land a couple of breakers with the power off, after he tested it, him standing right there. Probably why I liked it lol.' where id = 'e6c1c703-dbca-5388-969c-229ca14b3961' and seed_batch_id = 'fm-2026-10' and body = 'Mostly watching. On the electrical one he had me land a couple of breakers with the power off, after he tested it, him standing right there. Probably why I liked it lol.';  -- T042/r13
update replies set body = 'Will do. From what people told me, it is mostly about you and your work, but I am not sure. I will report back after.' where id = '14c5b8d0-0cdd-5cc9-8f1f-732a324c18b8' and seed_batch_id = 'fm-2026-10' and body = 'From what people told me, mostly about you and your work, but I am not sure. I will report back after.';  -- T051/r4
update replies set body = 'update: had it. Mine felt like mostly questions about my work and why electrical. I talked about a service change we did in Throggs Neck and the time I mislabeled a panel. Felt okay. Now I wait again. Appreciate everyone here, and my mentor especially.' where id = 'b5a7bdb8-fe22-55c7-a3c7-887e7777cb64' and seed_batch_id = 'fm-2026-10' and body = 'update: had it. Mine felt like mostly questions about my work and why electrical. I talked about a service change we did in Throggs Neck and the time I mislabeled a panel. Felt okay. Now I wait again. Appreciate everyone here, and dreb especially.';  -- T051/r7
update replies set body = 'Still in school in Queens, just reading all of this. There''s an IBEW foreman on here who answers everybody, so I''m getting a lot of good advice already.' where id = 'f8310562-d78f-5bf0-9762-b1545fb1acb2' and seed_batch_id = 'fm-2026-10' and body = 'Same as the Bay Ridge kid. Still in school in Queens, reading all of this. There''s a Local 3 guy on here who answers everybody, so I''m getting a lot of good advice already.';  -- T053/r16
update replies set body = 'Thanks everybody. Short version from all of you: keep working while you wait, apply anyway, and a second or third try is normal lol.' where id = '7e2fba30-3b0e-5614-806b-7d66ebbbd819' and seed_batch_id = 'fm-2026-10' and body = 'This blew up lol. Thanks everybody. Short version from all of you: keep working, apply anyway, check the official site, and non-union is real too.';  -- T053/r18
update replies set body = 'One I get every time: would I look at someone coming out of a warehouse with no field experience? Yes. Warehouse people know how to work a shift and follow a safety rule. Get your driver''s license squared away if it isn''t, take an OSHA 10 if you can, and apply. That''s more than a lot of applicants bring.' where id = '974fe93f-0b26-57b0-af6b-01111492d3a7' and seed_batch_id = 'fm-2026-10' and body = 'Yes. Warehouse people know how to work a shift and follow a safety rule. Get your driver''s license squared away if it isn''t, take an OSHA 10 if you can, and apply. That''s more than a lot of applicants bring.';  -- T056/r3
update replies set body = 'One I always get: does a vo-tech certificate count as the diploma? Usually not, they''re separate; the diploma is the high school credential, and the vo-tech certificate is extra. Bring both. Check the program''s list to be sure.' where id = '4a15506c-7e03-555b-80e6-9ca51ec8a4ad' and seed_batch_id = 'fm-2026-10' and body = 'Not dumb. They''re usually separate; the diploma is the high school credential, and the vo-tech certificate is extra. Bring both. Check the program''s list to be sure.';  -- T058/r3
update replies set body = 'theres a thread on here where a bronx electrician''s boss wanted two of his guys to have it for ptac units. so sometimes lol' where id = 'd8e81c22-fc67-5f23-a857-8b68e86a690c' and seed_batch_id = 'fm-2026-10' and body = 'theres a whole thread on that one, a 164 guy asked it in the summer';  -- T075/r14
update replies set body = 'Thank you all. So: it''s cheap enough to get anyway, and if one of these ever needs the sealed side opened, I''d rather be the one he sends. Signing up for Core and Type I.' where id = 'e799fe28-a476-5493-9590-f27f20fdd29d' and seed_batch_id = 'fm-2026-10' and body = 'Thank you all. So: installing doesn''t need it, repairing the sealed side does, and it''s cheap enough to get anyway. Signing up for Core and Type I.';  -- T080/r10
update replies set body = 'For anyone wondering about plumbing: the repipe day was good and the guy was great, my knees just weren''t. I didn''t light up the way I did on startup day. Maybe that''s unfair to plumbing.' where id = '543a0afd-5b97-550e-94f9-b1d47f20a56a' and seed_batch_id = 'fm-2026-10' and body = 'Honestly it was a day of drains. The guy was great. I just didn''t light up. Maybe that''s unfair to plumbing.';  -- T110/r5
update replies set body = 'Not unfair. One hard day on your knees would scare off plenty of people who''d make good plumbers. But you picked the day that felt right, and that counts for something. You can fake liking a job for a week, not for a whole career.' where id = '24d326d2-5958-5539-9e30-5a311005697a' and seed_batch_id = 'fm-2026-10' and body = 'Not unfair. A day of drains would scare off plenty of people who''d make good plumbers. But you picked the day that felt right, and that counts for something. You can fake liking a job for a week, not for a whole career.';  -- T110/r6
update replies set body = 'On the bump testing Marcus mentioned: first, follow the manufacturer''s calibration and bump-test schedule. It''s in the manual and it''s not optional. Second, a cheap meter that works beats an expensive one sitting in the truck. Third, if nobody knows when yours was last checked, assume it hasn''t been. Ask me how I know.' where id = 'bd1b9269-7de7-504c-b913-a9411a5b1e59' and seed_batch_id = 'fm-2026-10' and body = 'First, follow the manufacturer''s calibration and bump-test schedule. It''s in the manual and it''s not optional. Second, a cheap meter that works beats an expensive one sitting in the truck. Third, if nobody knows when yours was last checked, assume it hasn''t been. Ask me how I know.';  -- T115/r4
update replies set body = 'update on the super: he said i ''broke it'' when i was looking at it lol. the gas company guy told him it had been off the chimney a while. he shut up after that' where id = '37478ec8-db64-537c-8246-6da4e814f04e' and seed_batch_id = 'fm-2026-10' and body = 'he said i ''broke it'' when i was looking at it lol. the gas company guy told him it had been off the chimney a while. he shut up after that';  -- T115/r13
update replies set body = 'Yes, buy your own. You won''t always be standing next to your lead. And for the electricians reading: we spend plenty of time in rooms with fuel-burning equipment too, and the meter doesn''t care what trade you''re in.' where id = 'e03b8992-e7ac-53c1-9313-71188a6f1f49' and seed_batch_id = 'fm-2026-10' and body = 'Yes, you should. Electricians spend plenty of time in rooms with fuel-burning equipment, and the meter doesn''t care what trade you''re in.';  -- T115/r19
update replies set body = 'Can''t help on parking, it''s been years. What I remember from the city jobs I did back in my union days: deliveries are scheduled, usually early, with a loading area and a time slot for the hoist. Miss your slot and you wait half a day. The city teaches you patience whether you want it or not.' where id = '500f9330-7543-55bb-9e81-cc629eb5d543' and seed_batch_id = 'fm-2026-10' and body = 'Deliveries are scheduled, usually early, with a loading area and a time slot for the hoist. On the city jobs I did back in my union days, miss your slot and you wait half a day. The city teaches you patience whether you want it or not.';  -- T125/r5
update replies set body = 'Related, since it always comes up: what if the shop calls you salaried?
- Calling someone salaried doesn''t automatically mean no overtime
- There are rules about which jobs can be exempt, and a helper on a truck usually isn''t what people mean by that, as far as I understand it
Same answer: the Department of Labor, not me.' where id = '1b8ba55b-0fc2-5738-9b8d-d6d0d9e019fe' and seed_batch_id = 'fm-2026-10' and body = 'Not a dumb question.
- Calling someone salaried doesn''t automatically mean no overtime
- There are rules about which jobs can be exempt, and a helper on a truck usually isn''t what people mean by that, as far as I understand it
Same answer: the Department of Labor, not me.';  -- T134/r7
update replies set body = 'And for the no-refrigerant side jobs, like cleaning coils and changing filters for neighbors, it''s a smaller exposure but the same basic problem:
- You''re still uninsured if you fall off a ladder or break something
- "Just cleaning coils" turns into "while you''re here, can you look at this" fast
- Your boss may see it as taking his customers
Ask your boss if the shop wants the maintenance work. Usually they do, and you get the hours.' where id = '4197e370-3ca8-59d9-8fa8-eba2efca8312' and seed_batch_id = 'fm-2026-10' and body = 'Smaller exposure, same basic problem:
- You''re still uninsured if you fall off a ladder or break something
- "Just cleaning coils" turns into "while you''re here, can you look at this" fast
- Your boss may see it as taking his customers
Ask your boss if the shop wants the maintenance work. Usually they do, and you get the hours.';  -- T137/r2
update replies set body = 'And if you''re wondering why every owner says he''s broke when there''s a margin: some of them are. Two things:
- A lot of owners pay themselves last
- Equipment margins and service margins are very different animals
I''m not saying every owner is honest about it. I''m saying the $189 isn''t profit.' where id = 'be233b9b-3724-559d-96f0-5b2bb3997186' and seed_batch_id = 'fm-2026-10' and body = 'Because some of them are. Two things:
- A lot of owners pay themselves last
- Equipment margins and service margins are very different animals
I''m not saying every owner is honest about it. I''m saying the $189 isn''t profit.';  -- T153/r1
update replies set body = 'Attic work before 10 is going on my list. My boss also said nobody gets a medal for staying up there. Writing that on my tool bag.' where id = 'bb9fb586-3bca-56f6-bf33-0c7acb046106' and seed_batch_id = 'fm-2026-10' and body = 'Ordering the cooling towel. My boss also said nobody gets a medal for staying up there. Writing that on my tool bag.';  -- T173/r5
update replies set body = 'union city. service plumbing. hi lol, figured i was the only one' where id = 'd76f4ac6-933c-5f86-9fc1-fff405c56e4a' and seed_batch_id = 'fm-2026-10' and body = 'union city. service plumbing. hi lol, didn''t know there were this many of us';  -- T179/r2
update replies set body = 'Kearny, right on the line with Bergen, so I claim both counties like my father did. Good to see some Hudson people on here. If any of you ever want to talk old Hudson buildings, I''ve been in most of them.' where id = '03f5c62b-6fea-5c68-a979-6d08957109e0' and seed_batch_id = 'fm-2026-10' and body = 'Kearny, right on the line with Bergen, so I claim both counties like my father did. Good to see this many of you. If any of you ever want to talk old Hudson buildings, I''ve been in most of them.';  -- T179/r6
update replies set body = 'at least it''s not just me brother. and yes my handle says Kearny and I live in Bayonne. long story, don''t ask' where id = 'dac7eda6-c3c4-5028-918d-bc2fa9ba3f9b' and seed_batch_id = 'fm-2026-10' and body = 'more of us than I thought brother. and yes my handle says Kearny and I live in Bayonne. long story, don''t ask';  -- T179/r7
update replies set body = 'Honestly it''s simpler than it sounds. Both travelers come into the 4-way, and it either passes them straight through or crosses them over, so whichever way the other switches sit, flipping it changes which traveler is live at the far end. A 3-way can''t do that swap, which is why the middle one has to be a 4-way. Draw it: two 3-ways on the ends, the 4-way in the middle, and trace it with your finger in every position.' where id = '781c8970-969d-5cdf-b03f-7d5645ae0d63' and seed_batch_id = 'fm-2026-10' and body = 'Honestly that''s one of the better explanations I''ve seen. Draw it: two 3-ways on the ends, the 4-way in the middle, and trace it with your finger in every position.';  -- T188/r1
update replies set body = 'Good catch testing a fixture you''d been told was off. That''s the whole lesson. A Carter system is an old way of wiring 3-ways where the travelers carry the hot and the neutral, so with the light off both sides can be hot. I inspect in Jersey, not the city, so I won''t speak to the NYC code, but I''ve seen a couple of these in very old houses at the shore. The answer is the same: rewire it properly, don''t patch it.' where id = '2a615c67-9ce0-56fe-9187-20984ee6a507' and seed_batch_id = 'fm-2026-10' and body = 'Good catch testing a fixture you''d been told was off. That''s the whole lesson. I inspect in Jersey, not the city, so I won''t speak to the NYC code, but I''ve seen a couple of these in very old houses at the shore. Same answer: rewire it, don''t patch it.';  -- T190/r1
update replies set body = 'For the electricians wondering whether one ducted unit means less circuit work: it depends on the setup. A multi-zone outdoor unit usually powers its heads through the interconnect, so that''s one circuit to the outdoor unit. Three separate single-zone systems are three circuits. Follow the install manual either way.' where id = '057b4417-7e19-5746-943d-902aeffeea25' and seed_batch_id = 'fm-2026-10' and body = 'Depends on the setup. A multi-zone outdoor unit usually powers its heads through the interconnect, so that''s one circuit to the outdoor unit. Three separate single-zone systems are three circuits. Follow the install manual either way.';  -- T206/r6
update replies set body = 'And the question every customer asks, can you hide the linesets without it looking like spaghetti lol... lineset covers, run them on the back of the house, and talk about it before the install, not after. Some people hate the look of a head no matter what. Those are your ducted customers.' where id = 'fdf95284-452e-5401-8c2c-43ba2011305e' and seed_batch_id = 'fm-2026-10' and body = 'Lol the spaghetti question... lineset covers, run them on the back of the house, and talk about it before the install, not after. Some people hate the look of a head no matter what. Those are your ducted customers.';  -- T206/r8
update replies set body = 'On who actually does the tank work: mostly a separate company. On our commercial jobs it''s always a sub with its own insurance for that work. Here''s what I look for in that sub: their permits and paperwork, every time.' where id = '808ddaa0-459b-57b8-b0d2-af5492482b48' and seed_batch_id = 'fm-2026-10' and body = 'Mostly separate. On our commercial jobs it''s always a sub with its own insurance for that work. Here''s what I look for in that sub: their permits and paperwork, every time.';  -- T211/r13
update posts set body = 'A while back I posted about being 40 and unable to pick a trade. Kash has been mentoring me since then, and he helped me line up a ride-along in each trade, so here''s the report.

Plumbing: a day on a repipe in an old Colonial in Metuchen. Loved the problem-solving, hated my knees by 2pm.
HVAC: a changeout in a split-level in Edison in August. The attic was brutal, but the diagnosis part was interesting.
Electrical: a service upgrade in Highland Park, panel swap, PSE&G had to come out to pull the meter. That was the one where I lost track of time.

So I''m leaning electrical, and maybe the low-voltage side later because of my knees. Two questions: did anyone else pick partly because of their body? And is it crazy to plan around knees at 40?' where id = '74e792e7-756d-59ca-b879-631f095b9182' and seed_batch_id = 'fm-2026-10' and body = 'A while back I posted about being 40 and unable to pick a trade. Joy suggested ride-alongs, and she''s been mentoring me since, so here''s the report.

Plumbing: a day on a repipe in an old Colonial in Metuchen. Loved the problem-solving, hated my knees by 2pm.
HVAC: a changeout in a split-level in Edison in August. The attic was brutal, but the diagnosis part was interesting.
Electrical: a service upgrade in Highland Park, panel swap, PSE&G had to come out to pull the meter. That was the one where I lost track of time.

So I''m leaning electrical, and maybe the low-voltage side later because of my knees. Two questions: did anyone else pick partly because of their body? And is it crazy to plan around knees at 40?';  -- T042
update posts set body = 'Queens kid, still in an electrical program. Local 3 is the dream but everybody knows how hard it is. My aunt lives in North Bergen and said I could stay with her after I graduate.

I know jurisdiction is a "call them and ask" thing, which I will. But for the Jersey people: if I moved to Hudson County, would I just apply to whatever local covers there like anybody else? Is it dumb to move states for an apprenticeship? My foreman on weekends says I''m overthinking it.

edit: not trying to skip the line anywhere, just want options.' where id = '2874ad19-aa79-514a-8aac-a06236f2e60b' and seed_batch_id = 'fm-2026-10' and body = 'Queens kid, still in an electrical program. Local 3 is the dream but everybody knows how hard it is. My aunt lives in North Bergen and said I could stay with her after I graduate.

Dreb already told me jurisdiction is a "call them and ask" thing, which I will. But for the Jersey people: if I moved to Hudson County, would I just apply to whatever local covers there like anybody else? Is it dumb to move states for an apprenticeship? My foreman on weekends says I''m overthinking it.

edit: not trying to skip the line anywhere, just want options.';  -- T054
update posts set body = 'Sorry if this has been covered. After reading the thread on here about keeping a paper trail, I started keeping a log. Two years at my shop now, so I already feel behind.

Right now it''s a notebook: date, job, hours, what I did. Is that enough? Do I need my boss to sign something? Should I go back and reconstruct the last two years from my pay stubs, or is that pointless? I''d rather overdo it now than find out later it''s useless.

edit: I mean for a master plumber license someday, in NJ.' where id = '0f26629a-2668-55c4-9db1-9e20928d3863' and seed_batch_id = 'fm-2026-10' and body = 'Sorry if this has been covered. After reading the thread about what license you have when you top out, I started keeping a log. Two years at my shop now, so I already feel behind.

Right now it''s a notebook: date, job, hours, what I did. Is that enough? Do I need my boss to sign something? Should I go back and reconstruct the last two years from my pay stubs, or is that pointless? I''d rather overdo it now than find out later it''s useless.

edit: I mean for a master plumber license someday, in NJ.';  -- T073
update posts set body = 'About 7 months in at the shop out of Bayonne. Boss says starting next week it''s boiler cleanings and fall service every day until it gets cold, mostly old one-pipe steam in Bayonne and JC, some hot water. Ziggy told me to ask for one new thing a week so this is me asking ahead of time.

What actually happens on a fall service for an old steam boiler? What should I be watching so I''m not just the guy holding the light? brother I''ve seen maybe three steam boilers up close.' where id = '9c5f33f5-7dad-5095-8391-cd7aa070526b' and seed_batch_id = 'fm-2026-10' and body = 'About 7 months in at the shop out of Bayonne. Boss says starting next week it''s boiler cleanings and fall service every day until it gets cold, mostly old one-pipe steam in Bayonne and JC, some hot water. Joy told me to ask for one new thing a week so this is me asking ahead of time.

What actually happens on a fall service for an old steam boiler? What should I be watching so I''m not just the guy holding the light? brother I''ve seen maybe three steam boilers up close.';  -- T104
update posts set body = 'Update from the 40-and-undecided guy. After my first round of ride-alongs I leaned electrical, but Kash said to do a second day in whatever I was least sure about, so last Saturday I went out with an HVAC shop doing boiler and furnace startups.

The HVAC day was the one where I didn''t check my phone once. Ten houses, every one different, and the tech explained everything while he worked. My knees were fine in the basements. An attic in August would probably be another story.

For people who picked HVAC: what made you sure? And is the heat-season-then-AC-season thing as brutal as it sounds?' where id = '620e35ba-a7a2-5220-99e1-31e930bb0d5e' and seed_batch_id = 'fm-2026-10' and body = 'Update from the 40-and-undecided guy. After my first round of ride-alongs I leaned electrical, but Joy said to do a second day in whatever I was least sure about, so last Saturday I went out with an HVAC shop doing boiler and furnace startups.

The HVAC day was the one where I didn''t check my phone once. Ten houses, every one different, and the tech explained everything while he worked. My knees were fine in the basements. An attic in August would probably be another story.

For people who picked HVAC: what made you sure? And is the heat-season-then-AC-season thing as brutal as it sounds?';  -- T110
update posts set body = 'Different kind of question from me. We''re finally converting our own house in Piscataway from oil to gas: split-level, oil boiler with baseboard, hot water off a tankless coil in the boiler. Got three quotes and they disagree on the chimney.

Quote 1: new gas boiler and a new gas water heater, both into the chimney with a new liner.
Quote 2: high-efficiency boiler vented out the side wall in plastic, new water heater into the existing chimney, no liner.
Quote 3: high-efficiency boiler out the side wall, a separate sidewall-vented water heater, chimney not used at all.

Quote 2 is cheapest. Quote 1''s guy says Quote 2 is going to cause problems. Who''s right, and why does the chimney matter so much? Appreciate it. Kash told me to get more than one quote, so here we are. Still doing ride-alongs too, so this is half for the house and half for me.' where id = '7a7b79c2-0486-5e0a-b82b-f7fb83780cf2' and seed_batch_id = 'fm-2026-10' and body = 'Different kind of question from me. We''re finally converting our own house in Piscataway from oil to gas: split-level, oil boiler with baseboard, hot water off a tankless coil in the boiler. Got three quotes and they disagree on the chimney.

Quote 1: new gas boiler and a new gas water heater, both into the chimney with a new liner.
Quote 2: high-efficiency boiler vented out the side wall in plastic, new water heater into the existing chimney, no liner.
Quote 3: high-efficiency boiler out the side wall, a separate sidewall-vented water heater, chimney not used at all.

Quote 2 is cheapest. Quote 1''s guy says Quote 2 is going to cause problems. Who''s right, and why does the chimney matter so much? Appreciate it. Joy told me to get more than one quote, so here we are. Still doing ride-alongs too, so this is half for the house and half for me.';  -- T210
