  if n <> e then raise exception 'check failed: % (expected %, got %)', $q$select count(*) from posts where seed_batch_id is distinct from 'fm-2026-10'$q$, e, n; end if;
  execute $q$select count(*) from replies r join (values ('590990a1-4c85-50d7-90ad-f3ae44e360eb'::uuid, 'Appreciate all of this. Kash, the two-year math is the part I hadn''t actually done. Going to run real numbers, and ask around about seeing each trade up close before the end of the year.'), ('a5652ad7-d57a-56de-9e4c-6889feff8b89'::uuid, 'Universal is realistic if you study, even with zero background. Plenty of my 17-year-olds pass it. Do the practice tests until Core is boring.'), ('c6345d89-db21-5c3c-8221-6a3fbeb4af64'::uuid, 'update: asked for one new thing like zig said, the fittings on a repipe friday. boss let me do the whole manifold while he watched. leaked one. fixed it. best day so far'), ('fa46ee7a-dd27-5c8e-a17c-03a53433a816'::uuid, 'Careful with whatever number your school friend is comparing you to. If he''s heard of a 2nd-year non-union helper making $40 an hour in Central Jersey, that isn''t typical. Either that guy''s in the union and you''re hearing the total package, or he''s on a prevailing-wage job, or it''s a story. Comparing a cash rate to a union package isn''t apples to apples.'), ('34b3ef32-88ac-595f-8d8a-e4e3e7e91a1e'::uuid, 'On the first point, since it comes up every time, the short answer as I understand it:
- Home improvement registration is for general home improvement work
- HVACR work needs the HVACR license (or working under someone who has it)
- Check with Consumer Affairs for your situation; don''t take a contractor''s word for legal stuff, including mine'), ('7f4a5c6f-ed24-59dc-a265-b3a9319e4a31'::uuid, 'Montclair deli... ok now I know you''re all lost up there lol'), ('65c161fe-e92c-596a-a804-9e3f678f87ab'::uuid, '> Don''t let either side tell you the other one''s a scam

Fair. I didn''t mean my teacher''s scamming anybody. It''s the "dead end" thing that gets me, because my weekend guy clearly isn''t one.'), ('a97340b3-975f-5ffa-a6be-18a92eece5c6'::uuid, 'Since the first thing everyone asks is what changed: the interview. I had real jobs to talk about the third time. Before that I had nothing. And yes, I retook the test each time. Idk if that''s required everywhere, ask the program directly.'), ('63a042cc-4155-5c7d-98a8-6c89a4c7bc83'::uuid, 'For anyone wondering whether to bring up a third try: they knew. I said it before they could. Then I said what I did differently each year.'), ('9acc57e0-922b-5d67-b9af-054f1db5e4c3'::uuid, 'Thanks everyone, didn''t expect this many replies.'), ('e6c1c703-dbca-5388-969c-229ca14b3961'::uuid, 'For anyone wondering if they let you do anything on these: mostly watching. On the electrical one he had me land a couple of breakers with the power off, after he tested it, him standing right there. Probably why I liked it lol.'), ('14c5b8d0-0cdd-5cc9-8f1f-732a324c18b8'::uuid, 'Will do. From what people told me, it is mostly about you and your work, but I am not sure. I will report back after.'), ('b5a7bdb8-fe22-55c7-a3c7-887e7777cb64'::uuid, 'update: had it. Mine felt like mostly questions about my work and why electrical. I talked about a service change we did in Throggs Neck and the time I mislabeled a panel. Felt okay. Now I wait again. Appreciate everyone here, and my mentor especially.'), ('f8310562-d78f-5bf0-9762-b1545fb1acb2'::uuid, 'Still in school in Queens, just reading all of this. There''s an IBEW foreman on here who answers everybody, so I''m getting a lot of good advice already.'), ('7e2fba30-3b0e-5614-806b-7d66ebbbd819'::uuid, 'Thanks everybody. Short version from all of you: keep working while you wait, apply anyway, and a second or third try is normal lol.'), ('974fe93f-0b26-57b0-af6b-01111492d3a7'::uuid, 'One I get every time: would I look at someone coming out of a warehouse with no field experience? Yes. Warehouse people know how to work a shift and follow a safety rule. Get your driver''s license squared away if it isn''t, take an OSHA 10 if you can, and apply. That''s more than a lot of applicants bring.'), ('4a15506c-7e03-555b-80e6-9ca51ec8a4ad'::uuid, 'One I always get: does a vo-tech certificate count as the diploma? Usually not, they''re separate; the diploma is the high school credential, and the vo-tech certificate is extra. Bring both. Check the program''s list to be sure.'), ('d8e81c22-fc67-5f23-a857-8b68e86a690c'::uuid, 'theres a thread on here where a bronx electrician''s boss wanted two of his guys to have it for ptac units. so sometimes lol'), ('e799fe28-a476-5493-9590-f27f20fdd29d'::uuid, 'Thank you all. So: it''s cheap enough to get anyway, and if one of these ever needs the sealed side opened, I''d rather be the one he sends. Signing up for Core and Type I.'), ('543a0afd-5b97-550e-94f9-b1d47f20a56a'::uuid, 'For anyone wondering about plumbing: the repipe day was good and the guy was great, my knees just weren''t. I didn''t light up the way I did on startup day. Maybe that''s unfair to plumbing.'), ('24d326d2-5958-5539-9e30-5a311005697a'::uuid, 'Not unfair. One hard day on your knees would scare off plenty of people who''d make good plumbers. But you picked the day that felt right, and that counts for something. You can fake liking a job for a week, not for a whole career.'), ('bd1b9269-7de7-504c-b913-a9411a5b1e59'::uuid, 'On the bump testing Marcus mentioned: first, follow the manufacturer''s calibration and bump-test schedule. It''s in the manual and it''s not optional. Second, a cheap meter that works beats an expensive one sitting in the truck. Third, if nobody knows when yours was last checked, assume it hasn''t been. Ask me how I know.'), ('37478ec8-db64-537c-8246-6da4e814f04e'::uuid, 'update on the super: he said i ''broke it'' when i was looking at it lol. the gas company guy told him it had been off the chimney a while. he shut up after that'), ('e03b8992-e7ac-53c1-9313-71188a6f1f49'::uuid, 'Yes, buy your own. You won''t always be standing next to your lead. And for the electricians reading: we spend plenty of time in rooms with fuel-burning equipment too, and the meter doesn''t care what trade you''re in.'), ('500f9330-7543-55bb-9e81-cc629eb5d543'::uuid, 'Can''t help on parking, it''s been years. What I remember from the city jobs I did back in my union days: deliveries are scheduled, usually early, with a loading area and a time slot for the hoist. Miss your slot and you wait half a day. The city teaches you patience whether you want it or not.'), ('1b8ba55b-0fc2-5738-9b8d-d6d0d9e019fe'::uuid, 'Related, since it always comes up: what if the shop calls you salaried?
- Calling someone salaried doesn''t automatically mean no overtime
- There are rules about which jobs can be exempt, and a helper on a truck usually isn''t what people mean by that, as far as I understand it
Same answer: the Department of Labor, not me.'), ('4197e370-3ca8-59d9-8fa8-eba2efca8312'::uuid, 'And for the no-refrigerant side jobs, like cleaning coils and changing filters for neighbors, it''s a smaller exposure but the same basic problem:
- You''re still uninsured if you fall off a ladder or break something
- "Just cleaning coils" turns into "while you''re here, can you look at this" fast
- Your boss may see it as taking his customers
Ask your boss if the shop wants the maintenance work. Usually they do, and you get the hours.'), ('be233b9b-3724-559d-96f0-5b2bb3997186'::uuid, 'And if you''re wondering why every owner says he''s broke when there''s a margin: some of them are. Two things:
- A lot of owners pay themselves last
- Equipment margins and service margins are very different animals
I''m not saying every owner is honest about it. I''m saying the $189 isn''t profit.'), ('bb9fb586-3bca-56f6-bf33-0c7acb046106'::uuid, 'Attic work before 10 is going on my list. My boss also said nobody gets a medal for staying up there. Writing that on my tool bag.'), ('d76f4ac6-933c-5f86-9fc1-fff405c56e4a'::uuid, 'union city. service plumbing. hi lol, figured i was the only one'), ('03f5c62b-6fea-5c68-a979-6d08957109e0'::uuid, 'Kearny, right on the line with Bergen, so I claim both counties like my father did. Good to see some Hudson people on here. If any of you ever want to talk old Hudson buildings, I''ve been in most of them.'), ('dac7eda6-c3c4-5028-918d-bc2fa9ba3f9b'::uuid, 'at least it''s not just me brother. and yes my handle says Kearny and I live in Bayonne. long story, don''t ask'), ('781c8970-969d-5cdf-b03f-7d5645ae0d63'::uuid, 'Honestly it''s simpler than it sounds. Both travelers come into the 4-way, and it either passes them straight through or crosses them over, so whichever way the other switches sit, flipping it changes which traveler is live at the far end. A 3-way can''t do that swap, which is why the middle one has to be a 4-way. Draw it: two 3-ways on the ends, the 4-way in the middle, and trace it with your finger in every position.'), ('2a615c67-9ce0-56fe-9187-20984ee6a507'::uuid, 'Good catch testing a fixture you''d been told was off. That''s the whole lesson. A Carter system is an old way of wiring 3-ways where the travelers carry the hot and the neutral, so with the light off both sides can be hot. I inspect in Jersey, not the city, so I won''t speak to the NYC code, but I''ve seen a couple of these in very old houses at the shore. The answer is the same: rewire it properly, don''t patch it.'), ('057b4417-7e19-5746-943d-902aeffeea25'::uuid, 'For the electricians wondering whether one ducted unit means less circuit work: it depends on the setup. A multi-zone outdoor unit usually powers its heads through the interconnect, so that''s one circuit to the outdoor unit. Three separate single-zone systems are three circuits. Follow the install manual either way.'), ('fdf95284-452e-5401-8c2c-43ba2011305e'::uuid, 'And the question every customer asks, can you hide the linesets without it looking like spaghetti lol... lineset covers, run them on the back of the house, and talk about it before the install, not after. Some people hate the look of a head no matter what. Those are your ducted customers.'), ('808ddaa0-459b-57b8-b0d2-af5492482b48'::uuid, 'On who actually does the tank work: mostly a separate company. On our commercial jobs it''s always a sub with its own insurance for that work. Here''s what I look for in that sub: their permits and paperwork, every time.')) v(id, body) on v.id = r.id and v.body = r.body where r.seed_batch_id = 'fm-2026-10'$q$ into n; e := 37;
  if n <> e then raise exception 'check failed: % (expected %, got %)', $q$select count(*) from replies r join (values ('590990a1-4c85-50d7-90ad-f3ae44e360eb'::uuid, 'Appreciate all of this. Kash, the two-year math is the part I hadn''t actually done. Going to run real numbers, and ask around about seeing each trade up close before the end of the year.'), ('a5652ad7-d57a-56de-9e4c-6889feff8b89'::uuid, 'Universal is realistic if you study, even with zero background. Plenty of my 17-year-olds pass it. Do the practice tests until Core is boring.'), ('c6345d89-db21-5c3c-8221-6a3fbeb4af64'::uuid, 'update: asked for one new thing like zig said, the fittings on a repipe friday. boss let me do the whole manifold while he watched. leaked one. fixed it. best day so far'), ('fa46ee7a-dd27-5c8e-a17c-03a53433a816'::uuid, 'Careful with whatever number your school friend is comparing you to. If he''s heard of a 2nd-year non-union helper making $40 an hour in Central Jersey, that isn''t typical. Either that guy''s in the union and you''re hearing the total package, or he''s on a prevailing-wage job, or it''s a story. Comparing a cash rate to a union package isn''t apples to apples.'), ('34b3ef32-88ac-595f-8d8a-e4e3e7e91a1e'::uuid, 'On the first point, since it comes up every time, the short answer as I understand it:
- Home improvement registration is for general home improvement work
- HVACR work needs the HVACR license (or working under someone who has it)
- Check with Consumer Affairs for your situation; don''t take a contractor''s word for legal stuff, including mine'), ('7f4a5c6f-ed24-59dc-a265-b3a9319e4a31'::uuid, 'Montclair deli... ok now I know you''re all lost up there lol'), ('65c161fe-e92c-596a-a804-9e3f678f87ab'::uuid, '> Don''t let either side tell you the other one''s a scam

